<li about="#cite_note-Romer2-3" id="cite_note-Romer2-3" data-mw-footnote-number="3"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAVA"><a href="#cite_ref-Romer2_3-0" id="mwAVE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAVI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Romer2_3-1" id="mwAVM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAVQ">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Romer2_3-2" id="mwAVU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAVY">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Romer2_3-3" id="mwAVc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAVg">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Romer2_3-4" id="mwAVk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAVo">5</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Romer2-3" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt42" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAVs" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Romer"},"first1":{"wt":"David"},"title":{"wt":"Advanced macroeconomics"},"date":{"wt":"2019"},"pages":{"wt":"262–264"},"publisher":{"wt":"McGraw-Hill"},"location":{"wt":"New York, NY"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-1-260-18521-8"},"edition":{"wt":"Fifth"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRomer2019" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt42">Romer, David (2019). <i id="mwAVw">Advanced macroeconomics</i> (Fifth<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAV0"> </span>ed.). New York, NY: McGraw-Hill. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAV4"> </span><span class="nowrap" id="mwAV8">262–</span>264. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAWA">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAWE"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-260-18521-8" title="Special:BookSources/978-1-260-18521-8" id="mwAWI"><bdi id="mwAWM">978-1-260-18521-8</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Advanced+macroeconomics&amp;rft.place=New+York%2C+NY&amp;rft.pages=262-264&amp;rft.edition=Fifth&amp;rft.pub=McGraw-Hill&amp;rft.date=2019&amp;rft.isbn=978-1-260-18521-8&amp;rft.aulast=Romer&amp;rft.aufirst=David&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAD%E2%80%93AS+model" class="Z3988" about="#mwt42" id="mwAWQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SWJ-4" id="cite_note-SWJ-4" data-mw-footnote-number="4"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAWU"><a href="#cite_ref-SWJ_4-0" id="mwAWY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAWc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SWJ_4-1" id="mwAWg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAWk">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SWJ_4-2" id="mwAWo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAWs">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SWJ_4-3" id="mwAWw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAW0">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SWJ_4-4" id="mwAW4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAW8">5</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SWJ-4" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt45" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAXA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Sørensen"},"first1":{"wt":"Peter Birch"},"last2":{"wt":"Whitta-Jacobsen"},"first2":{"wt":"Hans Jørgen"},"title":{"wt":"Introducing advanced macroeconomics: growth and business cycles"},"page":{"wt":"vii"},"quote":{"wt":"...we apply and extend the modern AS-AD framework where the nominal variable is the rate of inflation rather than the price level, and where monetary policy is specified as a Taylor rule for the nominal interest rate. This set-up is gradually superseding the traditional IS-LM and AS-AD analysis and makes it easier to relate the model to real-world policy discussions."},"date":{"wt":"2022"},"publisher":{"wt":"Oxford University Press"},"location":{"wt":"Oxford, United Kingdom New York, NY"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-19-885049-6"},"edition":{"wt":"Third"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSørensenWhitta-Jacobsen2022" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt45">Sørensen, Peter Birch; Whitta-Jacobsen, Hans Jørgen (2022). <i id="mwAXE">Introducing advanced macroeconomics: growth and business cycles</i> (Third<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXI"> </span>ed.). Oxford, United Kingdom New York, NY: Oxford University Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXM"> </span>vii. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAXQ">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXU"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-19-885049-6" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-19-885049-6" id="mwAXY"><bdi id="mwAXc">978-0-19-885049-6</bdi></a>. <q id="mwAXg">...we apply and extend the modern AS-AD framework where the nominal variable is the rate of inflation rather than the price level, and where monetary policy is specified as a Taylor rule for the nominal interest rate. This set-up is gradually superseding the traditional IS-LM and AS-AD analysis and makes it easier to relate the model to real-world policy discussions.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Introducing+advanced+macroeconomics%3A+growth+and+business+cycles&amp;rft.place=Oxford%2C+United+Kingdom+New+York%2C+NY&amp;rft.pages=vii&amp;rft.edition=Third&amp;rft.pub=Oxford+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2022&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-19-885049-6&amp;rft.aulast=S%C3%B8rensen&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter+Birch&amp;rft.au=Whitta-Jacobsen%2C+Hans+J%C3%B8rgen&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAD%E2%80%93AS+model" class="Z3988" about="#mwt45" id="mwAXk"></span></span></li>
